WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.240
One true sentence goes into three tools.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.830
And the copier does what copiers do.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.710
Now there are three versions, and no original.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.170
Amplifier Data keeps the original once.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.010
Exact bytes, on a log that only moves forward.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:29.530
Each tool builds its own view, and every view points home.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:34.810
Lights out.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:35.790
Lights on.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.700
The original comes back, byte for byte.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.840
It’s a library for builders.

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:50.470
It keeps evidence honest; it doesn’t promise smarter answers.

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:57.610
Amplifier Data.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:00:59.010
Keep the evidence.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:00.210
Change the view.
